comments:
Thanks for more background on this Michael. It sounds to me like a good long-term investment to have more light-weight JSON encoding variants inside the standard Go package :). Is there any ticket opened for that (or could we file a one somewhere for looking into that) so we could track this? CC @dsnet.

Changing Go to solve the CRD watchers-related problem here would be pretty time-consuming, however. I'll probably try writing some POC with the solution @mborsz proposed in [here](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/110146#issuecomment-1289296713) related to caching `metav1.WatchEvent` inside the `cachingObject`. OTOH, this seems like an ugly entanglement of layers inside the apiserver logic and I'm not super excited about such a solution either.

@wojtek-t @lavalamp @liggitt any thoughts on that particular approach (or alternative ideas)?

We had a hackathon session with @tosi3k today and produced highly POC version of the change https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/compare/master...mborsz:exp_caching

Probably it's way too early to send this as a PR, but may be sufficient to show potential interface changes (especially runtime.CacheableObject) that may be necessary.

@wojtek-t what do you think about this changes? @tosi3k offered a help with cleaning this up if we agree that this direction isn't terribly bad.
